        {
          "_key": "0ib564ue",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Travelers consistently praise the underground access as \"surreal\" and \"the closest you can get to real Roman history,\" with many highlighting the cinematic feel of walking through gladiator corridors. The small group size receives frequent mention for enhancing emotional impact and allowing meaningful interaction with guides. The Arena Floor moment is regularly described as \"absolutely unforgettable\" with the 360-degree perspective being a standout feature. Some reviews note that the guided portion focuses on the Colosseum, with Forum and Palatine Hill being self-guided, though most appreciate the comprehensive historical context provided."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
